title: AND from NANDs
mode: draw
chapter: NAND does everything
check: behaves
parts: nand
---- intro
NAND is "AND, then NOT". To get a plain AND back, turn the NAND's answer round once more, and you built a NOT out of a NAND in the last lesson.
---- task
Build an AND gate out of two NAND gates: `y` is on only when both `a` and `b` are on.
---- start
input a 0 0
input b 0 60
led y 380 30
---- reference
input a, b
led y
y = a & b
---- answer
input a 0 0
input b 0 60
nand g1 120 20
nand g2 250 20
led y 380 30
a -> g1.0
b -> g1.1
g1 -> g2.0
g1 -> g2.1
g2 -> y
---- hint1
The first NAND gets `a` and `b`. Its answer is the opposite of AND.
---- hint2
The second NAND is a NOT: both its inputs come from the first NAND's output.
---- solution
NAND `a` with `b`, then feed that into both inputs of a second NAND, which turns it round. NOT NAND is AND.
---- done
Two NANDs make an AND. One more lesson and you have all three basic gates.
